| `src/store/meets.js` | Modify | `mutations.setMeetHistory` | New mutation to replace the whole history (used when restoring the persisted snapshot). |
| `src/store/meets.js` | Modify | `mutations.endActiveMeet` | History now de-duplicates by `meetId` and is capped to `HISTORY_LIMIT`, so "Recent" never shows the same room twice. |
| `src/store/meets.js` | Modify | `actions.init` | Restores the persisted history into state on startup, so the Meet view's **"Recent"** list (and the Wall) shows previous meets after a reload. |
| `src/store/meets.js` | Modify | `actions.endActiveMeet` | Persists the updated history to `localStorage` after a meet is torn down. |

### Notes
- **Root cause:** the Meet view already had a "Recent" block wired to `recentMeetHistory`, but `meetHistory` was memory-only, so past meets disappeared on reload and the list was empty in a fresh session.
- **Meet view unchanged:** it already renders `recentMeetHistory`; the data is now there reliably. No `src/views/MeetView.vue` edit is required.
- **Bonus consistency:** the Wall (`Wall.vue` → `basePosts`) reads the same `meetHistory`, so previous meets now also survive reloads there — matching the earlier "last meetings in the wall" change.
- **Scope:** history is stored per-browser (same pattern as `uiState` / `lastActiveProject`), independent of the backend. If you'd rather derive history from a server endpoint later, `loadMeetHistory`/`persistMeetHistory` are the single seam to swap.

