I'll add the profile avatar group to the wall event card and resolve the selected profiles (currently only plain names) into displayable accounts so the card can render them.

## 1. Analysis & Pre-Thinking

**Core Requirements**
- On a wall event card, when the event carries **profiles**, show them as a **DaisyUI avatar group**.
- The group must be led by the **project (or user) icon** on the left.

**Findings (grounded in the code)**
- `src/components/wall/wallEvents.js` → `chatToPost` already exposes `profiles: chat.profiles || []`, but a chat only stores profile **names** (`Chat.vue` → `onProfilesChanged` maps `selectedProfiles.map(p => p.name || p)`), so there is no avatar to render today.
- The project objects expose their loaded profiles through `$state.profiles` (used by `Chat.vue` → `profiles()`), which is where the avatar can be picked up; `project.project_icon` gives the project icon.
- `src/components/wall/WallPostCard.vue` renders the author, context label, body and attachment — but nothing for profiles.
- `wallEvents.js` already exports the deterministic avatar helpers (`avatarClass`, `initials`) used by `WallAvatar`, so the group can be rendered self-contained (no dependency on `WallAvatar`'s internals).
- The DaisyUI reference in the profile lists v5-only components (`status`, `list`, `filter`, `fieldset`), so `avatar-placeholder` is the correct modifier for the overflow chip.

**Strategic Approach**
1. Resolve `chat.profiles` (names) into displayable accounts in `wallEvents.js` (avatar from the project's profile list, initials fallback), and carry the project icon on the post.
2. Render an `avatar-group` in `WallPostCard.vue` led by the project/author icon, followed by up to 3 profile avatars plus a `+N` overflow chip.

**Dependencies & Risks**
- `post.profiles` changes from `string[]` to an object array — safe, the wall is its only consumer and it read it nowhere.
- Events without profiles (meets, notifications, local replies) render nothing (guarded by `v-if`).
- No layout change otherwise; only a new row under the context label.

**Target Files**
- Modify: `src/components/wall/wallEvents.js`
- Modify: `src/components/wall/WallPostCard.vue`

## 2. Minimum Changes Approach
Two focused edits: the mapping (resolve profiles + project icon) and the card (avatar group markup). No other component changes.

## 3. File changes

