## 4. File Change Summary Tables

| File Path | Action | Component / Section | Change Description |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| `src/utils/chatUnread.js` | Create | `isUnreadMessage`, `countUnreadMessages` | New shared pure helper encapsulating the "unread message" rule so the sprint task card and the activity wall agree on one definition. |
| `src/components/kanban/board/SprintTaskCard.vue` | Modify | `<script setup>` import + `unreadCount` computed | Reuses the shared `countUnreadMessages(this.task.messages, this.$user?.username)`. Behaviour-preserving — same rule, single source of truth. |
| `src/components/wall/wallEvents.js` | Modify | `chatToPost`, `buildPosts` | Imports `countUnreadMessages`; `chatToPost(chat, project, currentUser)` now sets `unreadCount` on each chat post; `buildPosts({ …, currentUser })` forwards the current username. |
| `src/components/wall/Wall.vue` | Modify | computed `basePosts` | Passes `currentUser: this.me?.username` into `buildPosts` so chat/task events carry the unread count. |
| `src/components/wall/WallPostCard.vue` | Modify | template + computed | Renders an unread `badge-error` (with a check-double icon, `title`/`aria-label`) and a subtle unread tint, **only** when the event kind is `chat` or `kanban` (`post.unreadCount > 0`). The reply action turns `text-error` while unread. |

### Notes
- **Why `kind` gating:** the request is scoped to *"if it's a chat or task"* — so only `chat` and `kanban` cards surface the badge; meets / PRs / notifications are unaffected.
- **Consistency & DRY:** the unread rule now lives once in `src/utils/chatUnread.js` and is consumed by both `SprintTaskCard` and the wall, so the badge behaves identically across surfaces.
- **Data limitation (pre-existing):** wall chats sourced from `chats.list()` may only carry the last message until fully loaded — same optimistic behaviour already documented in `SprintTaskCard`. The count therefore never over-reports and updates reactively once the chat's messages are in the store.
- **Accessibility:** the badge carries both `title` and `aria-label` ("N unread messages") so it is announced to screen readers, matching the existing `SprintTaskCard` pattern.

