## 5. Notes & Follow-ups
- **Unread root cause:** `Wall.vue` already passed `unreadOnly`, but `filterPosts` never read it — the post-level `unreadCount` (computed by `chatToPost` → `utils/chatUnread`) is now honoured. Because only posts with completed assistant replies addressed to the current user have `unreadCount > 0`, a wall made of your own brand-new posts will correctly show an empty "Unread" view.
- **Audio format:** the recorder prefers `audio/webm`, then `audio/mp4`, then `audio/ogg`, for the widest browser support; the blob is wrapped in a `File` and encoded to base64 exactly like image uploads (`ChatAttachment.fromFile`).
- **Mic permissions:** recording requires a secure context and mic access; failures fall back to a toast. The composer runs inside an iframe that already declares `allow="microphone *"`.
- **File picker:** the fix is to keep a broad `accept` and — critically — **not** set a `capture` attribute (which is what forces the camera). Left as a documented comment so it doesn't regress.
- **Follow-up (not in scope):** if audio notes should be transcribed or rendered by the `ChatEntry.vue` chat view too, the same `isAudio()` check can be reused there.

